--- utils -- standard library utility modules for the handl runtime.
---
--- This is an aggregator crate: it bundles many small modules (bool, fn,
--- math, mood, option, parse, serialize, typeof, encoding)
--- and re-exports modules from other crates (base64, hex, json, toml,
--- yaml, url-rfc, url-whatwg). The `str` contract is implemented by
--- `str-handl` and registered separately. The Rust Module/Function impls
--- live in plugin-lib-utils; this .hnl file declares the aggregated
--- interface surface (capabilities) for the plugin system.
---
--- The re-exported crates (base64, hex, json, toml, yaml, url-rfc,
--- url-whatwg) each have their own .hnl files declaring their own op
--- interfaces; they are registered here as concrete modules but their
--- capability declarations live in their respective data dirs.
---
--- ## bool module
--- bool.and -- logical conjunction of two booleans.
--- bool.or -- logical disjunction of two booleans.
--- bool.not -- logical negation of a boolean.
--- bool.xor -- exclusive-or of two booleans.
--- bool.nand -- negated conjunction (not-and) of two booleans.
--- bool.nor -- negated disjunction (not-or) of two booleans.
--- bool.implies -- logical implication (a implies b).
--- bool.eq -- test whether two booleans are equal.
---
--- ## combinators module
--- combinators.pipe -- pipe a value through a sequence of functions left-to-right.
--- combinators.flow -- alias of pipe: flow a value through functions left-to-right.
--- combinators.compose -- compose two functions right-to-left.
--- combinators.fanout -- apply a value to multiple functions, collecting results.
--- combinators.fanout_fn -- fanout returning a function for deferred application.
--- combinators.choice -- select between two functions based on a predicate.
--- combinators.apply -- apply a function to a single argument.
--- combinators.flat_map -- map then flatten one level.
--- combinators.find -- find the first element satisfying a predicate.
--- combinators.some -- test whether any element satisfies a predicate.
--- combinators.every -- test whether all elements satisfy a predicate.
--- combinators.group_by -- group array elements by a key function.
--- combinators.partition -- partition an array into satisfying/non-satisfying.
--- combinators.count_by -- count elements per key from a key function.
--- combinators.tap -- apply a side-effect function, returning the original value.
--- combinators.match -- pattern-match dispatch over a tagged value.
--- combinators.constantly -- return a function that always yields a constant.
--- combinators.flip -- flip the argument order of a binary function.
--- combinators.partial -- partially apply (curry) the first argument of a function.
--- combinators.when -- apply a function only when a predicate holds.
--- combinators.unless -- apply a function only when a predicate does not hold.
--- combinators.converge -- apply multiple functions to one input then combine.
---
--- ## transform module
--- transform.map -- map a function over an array.
--- transform.filter -- filter an array by a predicate.
--- transform.reduce -- reduce an array with a function and initial value.
---
--- ## math module
--- math.abs -- absolute value of a number.
--- math.add -- add two numbers.
--- math.ceil -- ceiling of a number.
--- math.clamp -- clamp a number between a lower and upper bound.
--- math.cos -- cosine of a number (radians).
--- math.cosh -- hyperbolic cosine of a number.
--- math.cbrt -- cube root of a number.
--- math.asin -- arc sine of a number.
--- math.acos -- arc cosine of a number.
--- math.atan -- arc tangent of a number.
--- math.atan2 -- arc tangent of y/x using signs of both arguments.
--- math.asinh -- inverse hyperbolic sine.
--- math.acosh -- inverse hyperbolic cosine.
--- math.atanh -- inverse hyperbolic tangent.
--- math.degrees -- convert radians to degrees.
--- math.div -- divide two numbers.
--- math.e -- Euler's number (e).
--- math.exp -- exponential function e^x.
--- math.factorial -- factorial of a non-negative integer.
--- math.floor -- floor of a number.
--- math.floor_div -- integer (floored) division.
--- math.fract -- fractional part of a number.
--- math.gcd -- greatest common divisor of two integers.
--- math.hypot -- hypotenuse: sqrt(a^2 + b^2).
--- math.infinity -- positive infinity constant.
--- math.is_finite -- test whether a number is finite.
--- math.is_infinite -- test whether a number is infinite.
--- math.is_integer -- test whether a number is an integer.
--- math.is_nan -- test whether a number is NaN.
--- math.lcm -- least common multiple of two integers.
--- math.lerp -- linear interpolation between two values.
--- math.log -- natural logarithm of a number.
--- math.log10 -- base-10 logarithm of a number.
--- math.log2 -- base-2 logarithm of a number.
--- math.map_range -- map a value from one range to another.
--- math.max -- maximum of two numbers.
--- math.min -- minimum of two numbers.
--- math.mod -- modulo of two numbers.
--- math.mul -- multiply two numbers.
--- math.nan -- NaN constant.
--- math.pi -- pi constant.
--- math.pow -- raise a number to a power.
--- math.radians -- convert degrees to radians.
--- math.round -- round a number to the nearest integer.
--- math.round_to -- round a number to a given precision.
--- math.sign -- sign of a number (-1, 0, or 1).
--- math.sin -- sine of a number (radians).
--- math.sinh -- hyperbolic sine of a number.
--- math.sqrt -- square root of a number.
--- math.sub -- subtract two numbers.
--- math.tan -- tangent of a number (radians).
--- math.tanh -- hyperbolic tangent of a number.
--- math.tau -- tau (2*pi) constant.
--- math.trunc -- truncate a number toward zero.
---
--- ## mood module
--- mood.ind -- inductive mood: project a value to a kind or error.
--- mood.int -- interrogative mood: test whether a value matches a kind.
--- mood.norm -- normative mood: project to a kind, returning a Result.
--- mood.pot -- potential mood: project to a kind, defaulting to null.
--- mood.neg -- negative mood: complement of a value w.r.t. a kind.
--- mood.cnd -- conditional mood: project to a kind with a default value.
---
--- ## option module
--- option.some -- construct a Some option wrapping a value.
--- option.none -- construct a None option.
--- option.is_some -- test whether an option is Some.
--- option.is_none -- test whether an option is None.
--- option.unwrap -- extract the value from Some, error on None.
--- option.unwrap_or -- extract the value or return a default.
--- option.unwrap_or_else -- extract the value or compute via a function.
--- option.map -- transform the inner value of a Some option.
--- option.flat_map -- map then flatten an option (alias: and_then).
--- option.and_then -- alias of flat_map.
--- option.filter -- keep a Some only if the predicate holds.
--- option.map_or -- map a Some, returning a default for None.
--- option.or -- return this option or an alternative if None.
--- option.or_else -- return this option or compute an alternative if None.
--- option.and -- combine two options, returning None if either is None.
--- option.xor -- exclusive-or of two options (Some only if exactly one is Some).
---
--- ## parse module
--- parse.parse -- parse a string with a named parser (url_rfc, url_whatwg).
---
--- ## serialize module
--- serialize.serialize -- serialize a value to a string with a named format.
--- serialize.deserialize -- deserialize a string to a value with a named format.
---
--- ## typeof module (type)
--- typeof.string -- type tag for strings.
--- typeof.str -- short type tag for strings.
--- typeof.number -- type tag for numbers.
--- typeof.num -- short type tag for numbers.
--- typeof.bool -- type tag for booleans.
--- typeof.null -- type tag for null.
--- typeof.array -- type tag for arrays.
--- typeof.arr -- short type tag for arrays.
--- typeof.object -- type tag for objects.
--- typeof.obj -- short type tag for objects.
--- typeof.any -- universal type tag (matches anything).
--- typeof.unknown -- unknown type tag.
--- typeof.is -- test whether a value is of a given kind.
--- typeof.must -- assert a value is of a given kind (error on mismatch).
--- typeof.may -- test whether a value may be of a given kind.
--- typeof.not -- test whether a value is not of a given kind.
--- typeof.when -- conditional type guard returning the value or null.
--- typeof.to_string -- coerce a value to a string.
--- typeof.to_number -- coerce a value to a number.
--- typeof.to_bool -- coerce a value to a boolean.
--- typeof.type_of -- return the type name of a value.
--- typeof.typeof -- alias of type_of.
--- typeof.identity -- return the value unchanged.
--- typeof.default -- return the value or a default if null.
--- typeof.coalesce -- return the first non-null value among arguments.
---
--- ## encoding module
--- encoding.encode -- encode a value to a string with a named codec.
--- encoding.decode -- decode a string with a named codec.
---
--- ## re-exported modules
--- base64 -- re-exported from plugin-lib-base64 (see base64/base64.hnl).
--- hex -- re-exported from plugin-lib-hex (see hex/hex.hnl).
--- json -- re-exported from plugin-lib-json (see json/json.hnl).
--- toml -- re-exported from plugin-lib-toml (see toml/toml.hnl).
--- yaml -- re-exported from plugin-lib-yaml (see yaml/yaml.hnl).
--- url_rfc -- re-exported from plugin-lib-url-rfc (see url_rfc/url_rfc.hnl).
--- url_whatwg -- re-exported from plugin-lib-url-whatwg (see url_whatwg/url_whatwg.hnl).
